# What EAS Build uploads to the build servers. When this file is absent EAS
# falls back to .gitignore, and that did NOT keep android/ out of the upload:
# the 2026-08-01 preview build shipped a 113MB stale app-debug.apk from
# android/app/build/outputs/ that was generated locally on 2026-07-25. The
# archive came to 560MB, and the builder emitted BOTH that stale debug APK and
# the real release APK, tarred together — so the artifact was a .tar.gz instead
# of an .apk you can actually download onto a phone.
#
# The native dirs are regenerated by prebuild on the builder and dependencies
# are installed there, so none of this needs to travel.
node_modules/
android/
ios/

# Local build output / caches
.expo/
dist/
web-build/
*.apk
*.aab
*.tar.gz

# Never ship secrets to the builder — EAS environment variables supply these
# (see `eas env:list --environment preview`).
.env
.env.*
